<title>JAPAN: Japan Nov zinc imports fall 49.7 pct year/year.</title>
<headline>Japan Nov zinc imports fall 49.7 pct year/year.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's refined zinc imports in November fell 49.7 percent to 3,324 tonnes from 6,604 tonnes in the same month a year earlier, Ministry of Finance data released on Thursday showed.</p>
<p>Figures were as follows (in tonnes):</p>
<p>			 Nov 96   Oct 96	 Nov 95</p>
<p> Total		 3,324     5,420	 6,604</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> China		 1,044     2,493	  4,340</p>
<p>Refined zinc imports in the first 11 months of 1996 were 130,106 tonnes, up 20.5 percent from 107,983 tonnes in the year-ago period.</p>
<p>--Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3-3432-6179</p>
